# Extroc configuration. Copy this file to .env.local in this directory and
# edit it. `cp .env.example .env.local`
#
# READ THIS FIRST, IT IS THREE LINES.
#
#   1. An empty .env.local is CORRECT and the app fully works: the
#      deterministic path answers every question through the same tools, the
#      same rules engine and the same grounding check the agent uses.
#   2. To turn on agent mode, set ONE key below. Leave the others empty.
#   3. If something is wrong, run `cd api && uv run crewops health`. It calls
#      the provider and tells you what to fix. Do not guess.
#
# The repository root, api/ and web/ are all searched, and .env.local is read
# before .env. A variable already set in your real environment beats both, so
# check `env | grep OLLAMA` if the app ignores what you put in here.
#
# NEVER PUT A PLACEHOLDER IN A KEY. A provider is selected by a variable
# HAVING A VALUE, so ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-key-here selects Anthropic and
# then fails to authenticate on every single turn. Recognised placeholders
# (your-key-here, changeme, todo, xxxx, <...>) are skipped and named in
# `crewops health`, but the safe habit is to leave the line empty.


# ============================================================================
# 1. PICK ONE PROVIDER
# ============================================================================
# Selection order is Anthropic, then OpenAI, then Ollama, by presence. The
# first one with a real value wins.

# ---- Option A: Anthropic. The recommended setup, and the fastest to get
# working. Nothing to install, nothing to run.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- Option B: OpenAI.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---- Option C: Ollama. TWO DIFFERENT SETUPS, DO NOT MIX THEM UP. This is
# where every reported setup failure has come from.
#
#   C1. OLLAMA CLOUD: set OLLAMA_API_KEY. You still need the local `ollama`
#       binary running (`ollama serve`), because it proxies to the cloud, but
#       you do NOT need to download the model. Default model is
#       deepseek-v4-flash:cloud, which is measured and is the one this project
#       has been developed against.
#         ollama signin          # then copy the key from ollama.com/settings
#
#   C2. LOCAL OLLAMA ONLY: set OLLAMA_HOST and leave OLLAMA_API_KEY empty.
#       The model then has to be one YOU HAVE PULLED. The default becomes
#       qwen3:8b, which is a starting point and not a measured choice, so
#       expect to set CREWOPS_MODEL:
#         ollama list                    # what you already have
#         ollama pull qwen3:8b           # or whatever you prefer
#       A ":cloud" model is served by Ollama Cloud. Asking a local daemon for
#       one is the
#         ResponseError: model '...:cloud' not found (status code: 404)
#       that people keep hitting. It means "you asked a local daemon for a
#       cloud model", not "your install is broken".
OLLAMA_API_KEY=
OLLAMA_HOST=

# Force one provider and skip the order above. One of: anthropic, openai,
# ollama, none. `none` proves the deterministic path on a machine that does
# have a key. Leave empty to auto-select.
CREWOPS_LLM_PROVIDER=


# ============================================================================
# 2. MODEL. All optional, each falls back to the provider's own default.
# ============================================================================
# Defaults per provider:
#   anthropic  claude-sonnet-5
#   openai     gpt-4.1                  (a starting point, not a measurement)
#   ollama     deepseek-v4-flash:cloud  with OLLAMA_API_KEY
#              qwen3:8b                 with OLLAMA_HOST alone
#
# Whatever you pick MUST SUPPORT TOOL CALLING. The agent binds 24 tools, and a
# model that cannot call them produces an answer with no evidence, which the
# grounding check then rejects. A 7B model is usually not enough.
CREWOPS_MODEL=

# A separate, usually cheaper, model for the planning step only. Falls back to
# CREWOPS_MODEL.
CREWOPS_PLAN_MODEL=

# Output token ceilings.
CREWOPS_MAX_TOKENS=
CREWOPS_PLAN_MAX_TOKENS=


# ============================================================================
# 3. BUDGETS. All optional. The defaults are the measured ones.
# ============================================================================
# Tool round trips one turn may take before it has to answer anyway.
CREWOPS_MAX_TOOL_ITERATIONS=

# Milliseconds before a turn is cut off. The problem statement is explicit
# that a 45 second response is not a decision aid. Defaults to 30000, and a
# budget set just under the line it is respecting is not a budget: do not
# raise it.
CREWOPS_TURN_BUDGET_MS=

# How many times the grounding check may send a draft back for a figure it
# could not attest, before the turn is refused instead.
CREWOPS_MAX_REPAIRS=


# ============================================================================
# 4. STORAGE
# ============================================================================
# Where conversation turns are logged as SQLite. Defaults to
# api/.crewops/memory.db, created on first run.
CREWOPS_MEMORY_DB=


# ============================================================================
# 5. VOICE
# ============================================================================
# Voice is a peripheral, not a second brain. Speech in becomes a question
# through the same /api/chat, and speech out reads back prose the verifier
# already passed. These keys buy a microphone and a voice; they do not change
# who answers, and nothing here can put a figure on screen. See docs/VOICE.md.
#
# Optional. With none of it set, the console is text only and everything else
# still works.
CREWOPS_VOICE_PROVIDER=sarvam
SARVAM_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Model and voice overrides. Each falls back to the provider's own default.
# CREWOPS_SARVAM_STT_MODEL=saaras:v3-realtime
# CREWOPS_SARVAM_TTS_MODEL=bulbul:v3
# CREWOPS_SARVAM_VOICE=shubh
# CREWOPS_GEMINI_STT_MODEL=gemini-3.5-transcribe-live
# CREWOPS_GEMINI_TTS_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview
# CREWOPS_GEMINI_VOICE=Kore

# Local VoiceKit, kept for offline development and disabled for hosting.
# CREWOPS_VOICE_LOCAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001
# CREWOPS_VOICE_LOCAL_VOICE=af_heart
# CREWOPS_VOICE_LOCAL_KEY=
# VOICE_OFFLINE=true


# ============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================================================
# Run this first, always. It calls the provider rather than reading the
# config, and prints the fix:
#     cd api && uv run crewops health
#
#   "Reachable: NO" plus "model '...' not found"
#       You asked for a model the provider does not serve. If it ends in
#       ":cloud" you need OLLAMA_API_KEY. Otherwise `ollama pull <model>` or
#       set CREWOPS_MODEL to something from `ollama list`.
#
#   "Reachable: NO" plus "Nothing answered at http://localhost:11434"
#       No Ollama daemon. Start it with `ollama serve`, or set
#       ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and forget about Ollama entirely.
#
#   "Mode: deterministic" when you are certain you set a key
#       Read the "Why" row: it names every env file that was read and every
#       value skipped as a placeholder. A variable already exported in your
#       shell beats the file.
#
#   Connection refused from the web UI, not from the model
#       That is the API, not the provider. Start it: `make dev`, or
#       `cd api && uv run uvicorn --factory crewops.server.app:create_app
#       --port 8000`. The UI expects it on :8000.
